  "id": "sex-identity",
  "term": "sex identity",
  "definition": "Sex identity is a child’s developing subjective sense of self as female or male. In this source, it is described as emerging from early caregiver-infant interactions, becoming more clearly subjective around 18 months, and growing more stable by about 3 years of age.",
